Jon Favreau's The Jungle Book released  this weekend and while King Louie might  be hungry for man's red fire  it appears that Disney are more than  satisfied with man's green cash I'm  Simon and trust in me with your jungle  news update Disney's new movie The  Jungle Book has swung to the top of the  box office this weekend the film which  mixes live action with cutting-edge 3d  animation has scored the second highest  ever  April opening pulling in a massive 100  and 3.6 million dollars the weekend  gross goes beyond the estimated figures  which as Collider notes had the film  topping out at a maximum of 85 million  dollars the film is now second only to  Furious 7 in terms of an April opening  worldwide it has to date made 290 point  9 million dollars the film which is  directed by Iron Man's Jon Favreau and  based on the classic stories of Roger  Kipling has been backed by extremely  strong reviews and much acclaim for its  use of 3d and CGI the all-star voice  cast includes Bill Murray Ben Kingsley  Idris Elba Lupita Nyong'o Scarlett  Johansson and Christopher Walken plus  newcomer Neel Sethi as Mowgli The Jungle  Book is the latest classic fairy tale  that Disney is retold for modern  audiences Tim Burton's Alice in  Wonderland earned more than 1 billion  dollars in 2010 and a sequel is due in  cinemas next month further down the line  Beauty and the Beast starring Emma  Watson is set for release in March 2017  what the success of the jungle book  means for the rival adaptation from  Warner is unclear that film has already  been moved back in entire year to  October 2018 and a report in variety  quotes a source as saying that the  popularity of the Disney film could  spell disaster for the Warner version  would you like to see Warner's  interpretation of the classic Jungle  Book story or would you rather see a  sequel to Jon Favreau's vision let me  know in the comments below or find me on  Twitter I'm at the J g'nort thanks for  watching and for all your entertainment  news keep it gamespot
 

